## 1. Core Principles & Angular Geometry

The core premise of the framework is that price displacement and time elapsed can be normalized into a shared circular coordinate system ($360^\circ$).

### A. Harmonic Cycle Divisions
* **Full Cycle ($360^\circ$):** Represents one complete rotational period.
* **First Harmonic Quadrant ($90^\circ$):** $\frac{1}{4}$ of the circle ($0.25$).
* **Second Harmonic Opposition ($180^\circ$):** $\frac{1}{2}$ of the circle ($0.50$).
* **Third Harmonic Quadrant ($270^\circ$):** $\frac{3}{4}$ of the circle ($0.75$).

### B. Modular Cycle Normalization
When projecting forward from an angular coordinate $\theta_0$ by a displacement $\Delta \theta$, raw values exceeding $360^\circ$ must be normalized back to the range $[0^\circ, 360^\circ)$:

$$\theta_{\text{normalized}} = \theta_{\text{raw}} \pmod{360^\circ}$$

