$$\omega_{\text{diurnal}} = \frac{360^\circ}{24 \text{ hours}} = 15^\circ/\text{hour} \quad (1^\circ \text{ every } 4 \text{ minutes})$$

To convert a harmonic displacement angle $\Delta \theta$ into an intraday forward time interval $\Delta t$:

$$\Delta t \text{ (hours)} = \frac{\Delta \theta}{15^\circ/\text{hour}}$$

$$\text{Projected Time Window} = T_{\text{anchor}} + \Delta t$$

