## 5. Methodology 4: Gann Square of Nine in Square Root Space

### Mathematical Concept
In Gann's Square of Nine spiral, angular movements around the wheel are represented as an arithmetic progression in square root space:
* $360^\circ$ full rotation $= +2.0$ added to $\sqrt{\text{Price}}$
* $180^\circ$ half rotation $= +1.0$ added to $\sqrt{\text{Price}}$
* $90^\circ$ quarter rotation $= +0.50$ added to $\sqrt{\text{Price}}$
* $45^\circ$ eighth rotation $= +0.25$ added to $\sqrt{\text{Price}}$

### General Formula
$$\text{Projected Level} = \left( \sqrt{P_{\text{base}}} \pm \frac{\theta^\circ}{180^\circ} \right)^2$$

Where:
* $+$ is used when projecting upward from a swing low.
* $-$ is used when projecting downward from a swing high.

### Price & Time Confluence
Vertical Fibonacci bar counters ($21, 34, 55, 89 \dots$) are projected along the horizontal time axis. Where a vertical Fibonacci time line coincides with a calculated Square of 9 horizontal level, a **Price-Time Confluence Zone** is identified.

